      en: "The Port of Skikda, located in eastern Algeria, is one of the nation's most critical industrial hubs, serving as a primary terminal for oil and gas exports. It hosts one of the largest oil refineries in Africa and significant facilities for liquefied natural gas (LNG) production. The port's strategic location on the Mediterranean coast allows for direct energy supplies to European markets. Beyond the petrochemical sector, the port handles substantial volumes of general cargo, including grain and construction materials. In recent years, massive investments have been made to modernize loading terminals and expand storage capacities to enhance export efficiency. Skikda acts as a major terminus for national pipelines transporting raw resources from the Sahara to the north. The Skikda industrial zone remains a vital pillar of the Algerian economy and a significant driver for regional economic development.",
